hero# Welcome to Doctor
 desc# A single-file documentation language that compiles to clean HTML for GitHub Pages. No terminal required.

h2# Getting Started

p# Doctor is a **minimal** markup language designed specifically for documentation sites. Write your docs in `.doctor` files, commit them to GitHub, and they automatically compile to beautiful, responsive HTML.

alert#tip
 p# This entire workflow happens on GitHub. You never need to open a terminal or install anything.

h2# How It Works

list#
- Fork the Doctor template repository
- Edit `.doctor` files in the `docs/` folder directly on GitHub
- Commit your changes — GitHub Actions compiles and deploys automatically
- Your docs site goes live at `yourname.github.io/doctor`
end#

h2# Components

table# Component | Syntax | Description
 title | title# Name | Sets the page title
 nav | nav# Label | #href | Top navigation link
 sidebar | sidebar# Label | #href | Left sidebar link
 hero | hero# Title + desc# | Large header section
 heading | h1# h2# h3# | Section headings with anchors
 paragraph | p# Text | Body text with formatting
 code | code#lang ... end# | Syntax-highlighted code block
 table | table# Cols... end# | Data table
 list | list# ... end# | Bullet list
 alert | alert#type + p# | Info/warning/success/tip callout
 card | card# Title + desc# | Info card
 grid | grid#N ... end# | Responsive card grid
 divider | divider# | Horizontal rule
 image | img# src | alt | Responsive image
end#

